function tuneQuality(rawDt){
 if(g.state!=='playing'){perf.frames=0;perf.elapsed=0;perf.wait=0;return;}
 if(perf.wait>0){perf.wait-=rawDt;return;}
 perf.frames++; perf.elapsed += Math.min(rawDt, 0.2);
 if(perf.elapsed < 1.3) return;
 const fps=perf.frames/perf.elapsed;
 perf.frames=0; perf.elapsed=0;
 if(fps<34 && g.quality>0.5){ g.quality=Math.max(0.5, +(g.quality-0.18).toFixed(2)); applyResolution(); perf.wait=1.2; }
 else if(fps>57 && g.quality<1){ ...increase only maybe } 
}
```
Increasing: quality steps 0.1; on ultra-slow no oscillation? If at 0.5 and fps 20, no further change. If fps >57 at 0.5, increase to 0.6; may drop to 50, no decrease since >34. Good. If increase causes <34, decrease back and wait; could oscillate between 0.5/0.68? Add hysteresis: raise only if fps > 58 and quality<1, reducing quality only if <32. Fine.

Use `rawDt` actual (not clamped) but clamp to 0.2 to avoid huge.

